      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General protocol for 1–6: a methanolic solution (5 mL) of Ln(NO3)3·xH2O (1 eq; x = 6 for 1 and 2, x = 5 for 3–6) was added dropwise to a 15 mL methanolic solution of LH3 (1 eq) and tetramethylammonium hydroxide (2 eq) with constant stirring. Solid Ni(CH3COO)2·4H2O (1 eq) was added and the deep orange solution was stirred for 12 h. The volume was reduced to about 10 mL by rotary evaporation, filtered, and left undisturbed; slow evaporation afforded green block crystals after 2 weeks. For 1: LH3 (0.050 g, 0.209 mmol), Y(NO3)3·6H2O (0.094 g, 0.209 mmol), Ni(CH3COO)2·4H2O (0.052 g, 0.209 mmol), and Me4NOH·5H2O (0.076 g, 0.419 mmol) were used.",
