      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "χMT at 300 K is 4.7 cm3 K mol−1 (calc. 4.6 with g = 2.15) and falls to 4.19 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. χMT slowly increases on cooling to 5.03 cm3 K mol−1 at 50 K then more sharply to 5.88 cm3 K mol−1 at 10 K, then decreases below 10 K, consistent with ferromagnetic NiII–NiII coupling and NiII ZFS. Fit of susceptibility and magnetization (PHI): J = +5.2 cm−1, Ja = −0.09 cm−1, g = 2.15, D = 5.6 cm−1. Msat = 7.21 NμB at 2 K and 5 T. No χM″ maximum above 2 K under 0 or 1000 Oe.",
